From 95f5d34f657e2a2d002fca358aadbfb17d1fe6b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:06:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: monaco: switch the GIC to 4 interrupt cells

The Cortex-A55 and Cortex-A78C PMUs share PPI 7. Telling Linux which
CPUs each PMU serves takes a PPI partition phandle in a fourth interrupt
cell, which the GICv3 binding allows only with #interrupt-cells = <4>.

Switch the GIC to four cells and append 0 (no partition) to every GIC
interrupt specifier. No functional change: the decoded interrupts of all
DTBs built from monaco.dtsi are the same before and after, apart from
the added zero cell.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco.dtsi | 778 +++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 389 insertions(+), 389 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco.dtsi
index 395d32d36844..bbbc1b1327c8 100644
